From 662aefb6cc88d9baa7db785e70815e394a4fd179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:31:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip photolive compatibility support (port of upstream
 23fcbbe6)

Upstream rewrote LivePhotoImp.isDeviceSupportLivePhoto (its dump's
Lg0/j;->v()Z) to "const/4 v0, 0x1 / return v0". That helper has no
counterpart in this build: the dyper APK contains no
ro.product.camera.livephoto.support key, no LivePhotoImp /
isDeviceSupportLivePhoto symbol, and no reflective Process.getTotalMemory()
call, so the whole prop-bitmask + RAM-ladder + "_global" + supported-device
list probe simply does not exist here. Its ro.product.* reads are limited to
brand, country, cpu, locale, manufacturer, marketname, mod_device and model.
In this build the same decision lives in the per-device config class instead.

How that class is chosen at runtime (why a base-class edit is the right
place): smali_classes5/Dg/f0.smali i()Ldevice_common; does
Class.forName(Build.DEVICE).newInstance() through the hash switch in
smali_classes3/I8/c.smali a() - default branch = the plain name - and falls
back to a bare Ldevice_common; instance on ClassNotFoundException. "onyx" is
not one of the keys in LI8/a;->a, so this phone resolves to the real Lonyx;
class (top-level, smali_classes3/onyx.smali), and everything dispatches
virtually off Lv7/b;->e:Ldevice_common;.

The photolive probe is Ldevice_common;->P5()Z. Its callers are only live
photo paths: smali/com/android/camera/data/data/s.smali y(I)Z (Jacoco key is
literally isSupportVideoModeLivePhoto), VideoModule (3 sites),
module/video/x.smali and fragment/settings/CameraCamcorderPreferenceFragment.
The base body was "instance-of p0, p0, Ldada;" - one leaf device class in the
Lxiaomi_phone4; lineage, unrelated to the onyx chain
(onyx -> redmi_phone2 -> device_common) - so it returned false for every
device except that leaf. Forced to 0x1, which is the same "skip the
compatibility check" effect as upstream.

Deliberately not touched, with the reason:

* Lonyx;->P5()Z already overrides the base with 0x1, so on today's onyx
  instance this edit changes nothing observable. It matters for the bare
  Ldevice_common; fallback instance - i.e. exactly the "device is not in the
  support table" case upstream's patch was written for.
* Photo-mode LiveShot uses the inverted flag Ldevice_common;->y2()Z ("live
  shot unavailable"): base returns 0x0 and Lredmi_phone2;->y2()Z returns
  !instanceof Lonyx;, which is already 0 for this phone. Its consumers -
  features/mode/capture/b.smali (getLiveShotItemBuilder), TopBarUtils,
  L4/k.smali (pref_retain_live_shot) and Na/b - therefore already show the
  LiveShot entry. Rewriting y2 to 0x1 would switch it OFF for onyx, so it is
  left as is.
* The other guard on that same LiveShot branch, LE7/d;->g()Z, is already
  hardcoded to 0x1 in this dump.

Signed-off-by: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
---
 smali_classes3/device_common.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes3/device_common.smali b/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
index 61efecf8..f37ee508 100644
--- a/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
@@ -1394,7 +1394,7 @@
 .method public P5()Z
     .locals 0
 
-    instance-of p0, p0, Ldada;
+    const/4 p0, 0x1
 
     return p0
 .end method
-- 
